+## Not-doing
+
+- Demo-host self-heal mint on 401 (decision 6437, track 2); operators paste the new key into wp-admin Settings and use Test Connection.
+- ADR-012 key metadata columns `label` and `created_by`; those are owned by CRM-1.
+- Plugin auto-adopt of a rotated key; keep paste plus Test Connection.
+- Usage or quota display.
+- Signup and billing; a separate subscription task will own checkout, hosted billing portal access, entitlements, quotas, and webhook reconciliation.
+- Any schema change beyond `portal_rotations`, `portal_auth_events`, and `portal_identity_links`, added directly in `001_identity_schema.py` per greenfield policy.
+- No `/admin` tenant-email update route in this MVP; `/admin` has no tenant-email field or email-update route.
+- CSRF exceptions for cookie-authenticated `rotate`/`revoke`; those mutations require the per-session token and matching `Origin`/`Referer` (bearer-authenticated requests have no ambient credential and skip CSRF).
+- Changes to the API-key auth section of `docs/workbay/contracts/security.md`; the implementation lane adds the portal contract in the same slice without changing that section.
+
+## Assumptions + open questions
+
+- Clerk plan and cost are acceptable; the `e16-7-spike` handoff settles the session JWT claim names (`sub`, `email`, `email_verified`, `azp`, `iss`, `sid`), uses a Clerk user rather than an organization for the MVP, and records JWKS-outage behavior. [CARD-06]
+- Every tenant already exists; `primary_contact_email` is nullable with a unique index. First claim requires a normalized verified Clerk email to match an unbound tenant; subsequent access uses the bound `(issuer, subject)`. A changed email never rebinds a tenant. An unmatched, NULL-email, or already-bound tenant is `tenant_not_eligible` (403). Operator provisioning and account recovery remain outside the portal.
+- The DNS A record for `app.altcontext.com` is an operator action.
+- The 500 ms p95 target is an intake assumption, not an existing SLO.
+- RLS extension to `api_keys` is explicitly deferred; revisit if the portal ever gets its own DB role.
