+- A request carrying both a `__session` cookie and an `Authorization: Bearer` header is rejected `401 invalid_session` before any token is verified, regardless of either credential's validity, and writes no `portal_auth_events` row.
+- Required-at-boot configuration must fail fast [rg-008] (Release It! fail-fast config): `ACX_CLERK_ISSUER`, `ACX_CLERK_JWKS_URL`, `ACX_CLERK_AUTHORIZED_PARTIES`, and `ACX_PORTAL_CSRF_SECRET`. `apps/prototype-description-service/api/main.py::create_app` mounts the portal router and runs the portal settings validator at app construction. JWKS requests use bounded timeouts and cached keys; an unavailable verifier returns a distinct 503 without affecting `/analyze` [CARD-07][RES-13].
+- Auth-event writes are bulkheaded (Release It!): the `portal_auth_events` insert uses its own short-lived session, never the request session. If that insert fails, the response is still the intended 403 with its reason code, the failure is logged at ERROR with the reason code and no email/token material, and the request session is not reused.
+- The `ACX_PORTAL_TESTS_REQUIRE_PG=1` test mode must fail, not skip, when PostgreSQL is unreachable. The eval command must pass with zero failures and zero skips (`{"kind": "junit_counts", "max_failures": 0, "max_skipped": 0}`), and every `/admin*` path on the new app host must remain 404 [CARD-10].
