+## Settled implementation contracts
+
+These contracts are binding for this plan and must agree with the sibling scope and eval files. Do not re-decide them in implementation lanes.
+
+- **`GET /portal/me`**: response is exactly `{tenant_id, email, key_count}`. The Clerk subject is not returned (privacy).
+- **`GET /portal/keys` history**: full history for the resolved tenant, including revoked rows with `revoked_at` set. Reads call `TenantBoundApiKeyRepository.list(include_revoked=True)` (no tenant argument; the bound `tenant_id` is applied internally). SC-2 names revoked rows explicitly.
+- **Tenant-bound repository**: `TenantBoundApiKeyRepository` is constructed with the server-resolved `tenant_id` and exposes no method that accepts a caller-supplied tenant id; it wraps `SqlAlchemyApiKeyRepository`. Isolation is proven at repository level (SC-30) because `api_keys` is RLS-exempt.
+- **Revoke concurrency**: direct revoke is one conditional `UPDATE api_keys SET revoked_at=now() WHERE id=:id AND tenant_id=:tenant AND revoked_at IS NULL RETURNING id` (DDIA lost-update/write-skew; do not read-then-unconditionally-write). Zero rows → re-read → 404 (foreign/missing) or 409 (already revoked); audit row inserted only when a row was returned, in the same transaction.
+- **Shared revoke service**: extract `recognition/interface_adapters/http/routers/admin.py::revoke_key_atomic` and its existing `RevokeOutcome(record, already_revoked)` into a tenant-aware service; `UnknownKeyError` stays the not-found signal. Adapters map independently: `/admin` keeps its shipped contract (200 with `already_revoked=true`, no second audit row); `/portal` maps `already_revoked` → 409 and `UnknownKeyError`/foreign key → 404.
+- **Dual credentials**: cookie+bearer together → 401 `invalid_session` before any token is verified, no `portal_auth_events` row, covering both-valid-different-principals and valid-cookie+invalid-bearer.
